35:["$","p","5",{"data-count":"","children":["Black soils have a thick, dark topsoil rich in organic matter ",["$","span","1",{"className":"cite","children":["(",[["$","span","liao",{"children":["",["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/references/#liao","children":"Liao et al. 2026"}]]}]],")"]}],", and the cold climate slows the microbes that break it down ",["$","span","3",{"className":"cite","children":["(",[["$","span","jiang",{"children":["",["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/references/#jiang","children":"Jiang et al. 2025"}]]}]],")"]}],", so it builds up. The gently rolling Songnen Plain suits large machines, and most rain falls in summer, when corn grows."]}]
36:["$","p","6",{"data-count":"","children":["However, the output comes more from scale than yield. Heilongjiang’s yield of 7.09 tonnes per hectare was only 6 per cent above the national average, and its share of China’s corn area (14.8 per cent) is close to its share of output ",["$","span","1",{"className":"cite","children":["(",[["$","span","hlj25",{"children":["",["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/references/#hlj25","children":"HPBS 2026"}]]}],["$","span","nbs",{"children":[", ",["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/references/#nbs","children":"NBS 2025"}]]}]],")"]}],". The soil damage on the next page may already be holding yields back."]}]
